{
  "title": "Common Aamal at Each of the Three Qadr Nights",
  "data": "Ghusl, Worship & Ziyarat\nBathe at each of the three Qadr Nights, preferably at sunset.\nSpend the whole three Qadr Nights in acts of worship.\nVisit the holy tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a) on these nights.\nRecite [Dua Jawshan al-Kabir](E29) at the three Qadr Nights.",
  "tabs": [
    "Prayers & Istighfar\nOffer a two-unit prayer, reciting at each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and repeating [Surah al-Ikhlas](A116) seven times.\nAfter finishing, repeat seventy times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFIRUL LAAHA WA ATOOBU ILAYH\nI implore Allah's forgiveness and I repent before Him.\nOffer the one-hundred-unit prayer, reciting in each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and repeating [Surah al-Ikhlas](A116) ten times.",
    "Dua with the Qur’an Open\nOpen a copy of the Holy Qur'an between your hands and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِكِتَابِكَ الْمُنْزَلِ وَمَا فِيْهِ وَفِيْهِ اسْمُكَ الْاَكْبَرُ وَاَسْمَاۤؤُكَ الْحُسْنٰى\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALUKA BI-KITAABIKAL MUNZALI WA MAA FEEHI WA FEEHIS MUKAL AKBARU WA ASMAAA-UKAL HUSNAA\nO Allah, I ask You by Your revealed Book and what is in it, and in it is Your Greatest Name and Your most beautiful Names,\nوَمَا يُخَافُ وَيُرْجٰى اَنْ تَجْعَلَنِيْ مِنْ عُتَقَاۤئِكَ مِنَ النَّارِ\nWA MAA YUKHAAFU WA YURJAA AN TAJ-A'LANEE MIN U'TAQAAA-IKA MINAN NAAR\nand what is feared and hoped for, that You make me among those You have freed from the Fire.\nOne may then pray for the fulfillment of one's desires.",
    "Dua with the Qur’an on the Head\nPlace a copy of the Holy Qur'an on the head and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بِحَقِّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ وَبِحَقِّ مَنْ اَرْسَلْتَهُ بِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA BI-HAQQI HAAZAL QUR-AANI WA BI-HAQQI MAN ARSALTAHU BIH\nO Allah, by the right of this Qur'an, and by the right of the one You sent with it,\nوَبِحَقِّ كُلِّ مُؤْمِنٍ مَدَحْتَهُ فِيْهِ وَبِحَقِّكَ عَلَيْهِمْ فَلَا اَحَدَ اَعْرَفُ بِحَقِّكَ مِنْكَ\nWA BI-HAQQI KULLI MU'MININ MADAHTAHU FEEHI WA BI-HAQQIKA A'LAYHIM FALAA AHADA A'RAFU BI-HAQQIKA MINK\nand by the right of every believer You have praised in it, and by Your right upon them — for no one knows Your right better than You.\nThen repeat ten times:\nبِكَ يَاۤ اَللهُ بِمُحَمَّدٍ بِعَلِيٍّ بِفَاطِمَةَ بِالْحَسَنِ بِالْحُسَيْنِ بِعَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ بِمُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ بِجَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ بِمُوْسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ بِعَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى بِمُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ بِعَلِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ بِالْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ بِالْحُجَّةِ\nBIKA YAA ALLAAHO BI-MUHAMMADIN BI-A'LEE-YIN BI-FAATIMATA BIL HASANI BIL HUSAYNI BI-A'LEE-YIBNIL HUSAYNI BI-MUHAMMADIBNI A'LEE-YIN BI-JA'FARIBNI MUHAMMADIN BI-MOOSAA IBNI JA'FARIN BI-A'LEE-YIBNI MOOSAA BI-MUHAMMADIBNI A'LEE-YIN BI-A'LEE-YIBNI MUHAMMADIN BIL HASANIBNI A'LEE-YIN BIL HUJJAH\nBy You, O Allah; by Muhammad; by Ali; by Fatimah; by al-Hasan; by al-Husayn; by Ali ibn al-Husayn; by Muhammad ibn Ali; by Ja'far ibn Muhammad; by Musa ibn Ja'far; by Ali ibn Musa; by Muhammad ibn Ali; by Ali ibn Muhammad; by al-Hasan ibn Ali; by al-Hujjah.\nOne should then pray Almighty Allah for the fulfillment of one's desires.",
    "Dua Amsaytu Laka Abdan\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَمْسَيْتُ لَكَ عَبْدًا دَاخِرًا لَا اَمْلِكُ لِنَفْسِيْ نَفْعًا وَلَا ضَرًّا وَلَا اَصْرِفُ عَنْهَا سُوْۤءًا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AMSAYTU LAKA A'BDAN DAAKHIRAN LAA AMLIKU LI-NAFSEE NAF-A'N WA LAA DARRAN WA LAA ASRIFU A'NHAA SOOO-AA\nO Allah, I have entered this evening as Your humble servant, having no power to bring myself benefit or harm, nor to turn evil away from myself,\nاَشْهَدُ بِذٰلِكَ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ وَاَعْتَرِفُ لَكَ بِضَعْفِ قُوَّتِيْ وَقِلَّةِ حِيْلَتِيْ\nASH-HADU BI-ZAALIKA A'LAA NAFSEE WA A'TARIFU LAKA BI-DA'FI QUWWATEE WA QILLATI HEELATEE\nI bear witness to that against myself, and I confess to You the weakness of my strength and the paucity of my resource,\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَنْجِزْ لِيْ مَا وَعَدْتَنِيْ وَجَمِيْعَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ مِنَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA ANJIZ LEE MAA WA-A'DTANEE WA JAMEE-A'L MU'MINEENA WAL MU'MINAATI MINAL MAGHFIRATI FEE HAAZIHIL LAYLAH\nso bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and fulfil for me — and for all the believing men and women — what You have promised of forgiveness on this night,\nوَاَتْمِمْ عَلَيَّ مَا اٰتَيْتَنِيْ فَاِنِّيْ عَبْدُكَ الْمِسْكِيْنُ الْمُسْتَكِيْنُ الضَّعِيْفُ الْفَقِيْرُ الْمَهِيْنُ\nWA ATMIM A'LAYYA MAA AATAYTANEE FA-INNEE A'BDUKAL MISKEENUL MUSTAKEENUD DA-E'EFUL FAQEERUL MAHEEN\nand complete for me what You have given me, for I am Your poor, humble, weak, needy, lowly servant.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْنِيْ نَاسِيًا لِذِكْرِكَ فِيْمَا اَوْلَيْتَنِيْ وَلَا لِاِحْسَانِكَ فِيْمَا اَعْطَيْتَنِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ-A'LNEE NAASIYAL LI-ZIKRIKA FEEMAA AWLAYTANEE WA LAA LI-IHSAANIKA FEEMAA A'TAYTANEE\nO Allah, do not make me forgetful of Your remembrance in what You have bestowed on me, nor of Your kindness in what You have given me,\nوَلَا اٰيِسًا مِنْ اِجَابَتِكَ وَاِنْ اَبْطَاَتَ عَنِّيْ فِيْ سَرَّاۤءَ اَوْ ضَرَّاۤءَ اَوْ شِدَّةَ اَوْ رَخَاۤءَ\nWA LAA AAYISAM MIN IJAABATIKA WA IN ABTA-AT A'NNEE FEE SARRAAA-I AW DARRAAA-I AW SHIDDATIN AW RAKHAAA-I\nnor despairing of Your response, even if it be delayed for me, whether in ease or hardship, in adversity or comfort,\nاَوْ عَافِيَةٍ اَوْ بَلَاۤءٍ اَوْ بُؤْسٍ اَوْ نَعْمَاۤءَ اِنَّكَ سَمِيْعُ الدُّعَاۤءِ\nAW A'AAFIYATIN AW BALAAA-IN AW BU'SIN AW NA'MAAA-I INNAKA SAMEE-U'D DUA-A'\nin well-being or trial, in misery or blessing; verily You are the Hearer of supplications."
