  "merits": "Ghusl: According to Allamah al-Majlisi, it is preferable to perform the bathing at sunset so as to be ready for the Isha prayer with a bathing.\n\nTwo-unit prayer: According to a Hadith reported from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), Almighty Allah will forgive whoever offers this prayer, and will forgive his parents, before he leaves his place.\n\nZiyarat of Imam al-Husayn (a): A Hadith reads that at the Qadr Nights, a caller from the heavens calls out from the Seventh Sky, and specifically from the center of the Holy Throne, that Almighty Allah shall forgive whoever visits the tomb of al-Husayn (a).\n\nSpending the nights in worship: A Hadith reads that whoever spends the whole Qadr Nights in worship will have all his sins forgiven, even if they are as many as the stars, as heavy as the mountains, and as weighty as the seawater.\n\nOne-hundred-unit prayer: it carries a remarkable reward.\n\nDua Amsaytu Laka Abdan: Al-Kaf'ami has narrated that Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a) used to say this supplicatory prayer very frequently at the Qadr Nights while sitting, standing, bowing, and prostrating.\n\nAllamah al-Majlisi has mentioned that the most favorable rite at the Qadr Nights is to implore Almighty Allah's forgiveness, to mention Him, and to pray for the settlement of one's worldly and religious affairs as well as for one's parents, relatives, and brethren-in-faith — the dead and the living — and to invoke blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household.\n\nDua Jawshan al-Kabir: According to some narrations, it is recommended to recite [Dua Jawshan al-Kabir](E29) at the three Qadr Nights.\n\nIt has also been narrated that when the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) was asked about the best prayer to say on the Qadr Night, he said, \"Pray for good health.\""
